      "description": "Career Services | Northern State University in South Dakota Skip to main content SEARCH VISIT myNSU APPLY GIVE REQUEST INFORMATION Admissions Apply Visit Admitted Students Degree Programs Undergraduate Graduate Online Transfer Continuing Education Reentry International Huron Community Campus Dual Credit Financial Aid Apply Scholarships Tuition and Costs FAQs Forms Pay Your Bill Academics Academic Schools and College Academic Affairs Undergraduate Studies Graduate Studies High School Programs Honors Program International Programs Degree Programs Research Records and Registration Course Catalog Library Degree Programs Athletics Student Life Residence Life Dining Services Health and Wellness Student Involvement Student Success Center Student Affairs Campus Safety Concerns and Complaints Wolf Shoppe About Campus Office of the President Presidential Investiture Strategic Plan Employee Directory Departments and Offices Gypsy Days NSU Foundation Community of Aberdeen Accreditation Consumer Information Event Planning at Northern Points of Pride Policies Image Access valuable professional resources, the Wolf Work job board and trained career advisors. Residence Life Dining Services Health and Wellness Accessibility Services Counseling Services Recreation and Intramurals Student Health Services Student Wellness and Prevention Dimensions of Wellness Student Involvement New Student Programs Wolf Pack Welcome Student Success Center Academic Advising Academic Support American Indian Circle Program Career Services Military Veteran Affairs Navigate360 Student Overview Supplemental Instruction TRIO McNair Scholars Program TRIO Student Support Services TRIO Upward Bound Testing Services Tutoring Services Student Affairs Student Rights and Responsibilities Title IX Campus Safety Concerns and Complaints Wolf Shoppe Career Services Home Student Life Student Success Center Career Services Welcome to NSU Career Services We prepare students for lifelong success. Unleash your professional potential with the help of Northern State University's Career Services Office. Wherever you are in your academic or professional journey, Northern is here to help you succeed with professional development workshops, individualized career appointments, and community job and graduate school fairs. Build your skillset through career-related learning, gain experience with internships throughout the Aberdeen community and region, and connect with NSU alumni who are eager to support the newest generation of Wolves. Career Services are available to undergraduate and graduate students, with select services available to NSU alumni. For details, see Institutional Research or contact NSU Career Services . “One thing I like about NSU is the many resources available to students such as the Tutoring Center; Career Services; and, being an international student, the International Office. All of these have helped tremendously to shape my experience here by offering help when needed.” Shanice Burrell, Buff Bay, Jamaica Upcoming Events For Students Schedule an Appointment on Navigate Meet one-on-one with a career advisor to explore degree paths, connect with internship opportunities, polish your resume or prep for an interview. Success-Building Workshop Gain skills for better studying and test-taking, as well as networking for your future career with our Student Success Gold Series workshops. Attend an upcoming workshop Employment Opportunities Discover available on- and off-campus job positions, internships and full-time positions with NSU's online employment database, Wolf Work. Access Wolf Work Career Fairs Network with employers and professionals in your field from the Aberdeen community. Attend mini-sessions for organizations you're interested in, and discover internship and job opportunities. Register for the next career fair Career Resources Helpful Links UTK's Center for Career Development & Academic Exploration For Alumni Employment Opportunities Share and manage available job postings for internships and part-time and full-time positions with Northern State University's online employment database, Wolf Work. Even after graduation, you'll have lifetime access to Northern's online employment database, Wolf Work. Find internships and part-time and full-time positions in your region. Access Wolf Work Career Fairs Make connections in the community and meet others in your field at one of Northern's annual career fairs. As an alum, you can attend free of charge and get access to professional opportunities. Register for the next career fair For Employers Job Postings Share and manage available job postings for internships and part-time and full-time positions with Northern State University's online employment database, Wolf Work. Access Wolf Work Career Fairs Share and manage available job postings for internships and part-time and full-time positions with Northern State University's online employment database, Wolf Work. Access Wolf Work Recruitment Activities Grow your business and meet potential employees through recruitment activities such as tabling opportunities, presentations and mock interviews with students. Set up a recruitment session Meet our Staff Carly Bierman Career Services Coordinator Contact Me MeWaldt-Jensen 102B 605-626-2416 carly.bierman@northern.edu Residence Life Dining Services Health and Wellness Accessibility Services Counseling Services Recreation and Intramurals Student Health Services Student Wellness and Prevention Dimensions of Wellness Student Involvement New Student Programs Wolf Pack Welcome Student Success Center Academic Advising Academic Support American Indian Circle Program Career Services Military Veteran Affairs Navigate360 Student Overview Supplemental Instruction TRIO McNair Scholars Program TRIO Student Support Services TRIO Upward Bound Testing Services Tutoring Services Student Affairs Student Rights and Responsibilities Title IX Campus Safety Concerns and Complaints Wolf Shopp